# Deferred Docker Packaging - Final Stage

Status: NOT_STARTED
Milestone: M6 Optional final-stage containerization
Dependencies: 17_RELEASE_ACCEPTANCE.todo

## Purpose

Package the already-working native Python speech service in a container only after the core
application is complete. Docker must never be required for ordinary transcription.

## Tasks

- [x] Record corrected owner direction: native C# plus Python first, containerization at the absolute end.
- [x] Keep protocol/model/token interfaces independent of the deployment host.
- [x] Add non-root Docker recipe, loopback-published Compose service, read-only model and health check.
- [x] Exclude notes/audio/tokens/models from source and Docker contexts.
- [x] Preserve optional Docker recipes without putting them on native startup or release prerequisites.
- [ ] Run actual Docker build/start/readiness/offline-inference/stop tests on an available engine.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Optional container inference works without internet after explicit model setup.
- [ ] No microphone/desktop access or credentials are baked into the container.
- [ ] Service is authenticated, loopback-only on the host, resource-bounded, and stores no audio.
- [ ] Actual container behavior is evidenced separately from native Python execution.
- [ ] Optional Docker packaging is documented as separate from normal native Python startup.

## Completion evidence

- Docker CLI/engine unavailable on this machine at implementation start.
- A native service test will not be relabelled a container run.
- October8 03:25 correction supersedes the earlier Docker-selected interpretation: Docker was intended
  only as eventual containerization, not architecture/runtime dependency. Native workstream22 owns startup.
- Docker recipe files exist, but their execution is deferred until after17. No Docker installation is
  needed to run the app, start recognition, test native inference, or complete the native release.

## Completion log

- 2026-10-08 - Added as required implementation; actual Docker execution depends on an installed engine.
- 2026-10-08 03:25 IST - Corrected to optional final-stage packaging; removed from native critical path.
